    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Flurry of Blows",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "flourish"
      ],
      "text": "Frequency once per turn\n\n---\n\nEffect The acolyte makes two unarmed Strikes, or one unarmed Strike and a dueling pistol Strike. If both hit the same creature, combine their damages for the purposes of resistances and weaknesses.\n\nThe acolyte's multiple attack penalty applies normally to these Strikes.",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 1,
        "per": "turn"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Sneak Attack",
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "The acolyte deals an extra 2d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "key": "damage-dice",
          "selector": "strike-damage",
          "dice": 2,
          "die": "d6",
          "category": "precision",
          "when": [
            "target:condition:off-guard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "roll-option",
          "option": "target:condition:off-guard",
          "toggleable": true,
          "label": "PF2E.SpecificRule.TOTMToggle.OffGuard"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Thousand Ants Stance",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "stance"
      ],
      "text": "The acolyte takes the stance of thousand ants, a style mimicking the distracting strikes of a swarm of tiny, vicious creatures. The acolyte can make thousand wounds unarmed attacks.\n\nThese deal 1d12 piercing damage; are in the brawling group; and have the backstabber, forceful, and unarmed traits. While in this stance, if the acolyte successfully Trips a target, the target is Off-Guard until the start of the target's next turn."
    }
